FILES
- lib/ai/extract-loan-statement.ts (new) - zod schema + extraction
- app/api/loan-statements/extract/route.ts (new) - upload, extract, stage
- tests/lib/ai/loan-statement-schema.test.ts (new) - 8 tests (106 total)

DESIGN DECISIONS
- Staged review, not trust. The row is created with confirmed_at null;
  the DB treats it as unclaimable until a human confirms. Mirrors
  staged_receipts.
- Store the document BEFORE extracting, and create the row even when
  extraction throws. The statement is the evidence the pack ships; losing
  it because a model call failed is worse than a missing figure the user
  can type in.
- PDF text layer preferred over vision, matching extractInvoiceFields.
  Lender statements are dense tables which read more reliably as text and
  cost far fewer tokens.
- Prompt explicitly excludes principal, redraw, offset balances and the
  loan balance. A statement shows all of these near the interest total and
  the wrong line would land in a return.
- Every field nullable: "not found" must surface as null, never as a
  fabricated number. confidence carries a rubric so 0.9+ means a labelled
  total was read directly rather than inferred.
- Model wiring via lib/ai/openai-client.ts per tech-stack.md, not at the
  call site.
- Upload uses the RLS-scoped client, so the storage prefix is the user's
  own and the loan_statements insert is authorised by
  has_property_write_access in the database, not by a check in the route.

VERIFICATION PERFORMED
- CI=true npm test -> 6 files, 106 tests passed. Schema tests assert the
  strictness that matters: a string "21450.32" is REJECTED rather than
  coerced (coercion would silently mangle a currency-formatted figure into
  a wrong number in a tax return); confidence outside 0-1 rejected;
  confidence and interest_paid keys required to be present even when null,
  so a truncated model response fails loudly rather than reading as "not
  found"; account masking preserved verbatim.
- npm run build -> Compiled successfully; the new route appears in the
  build output (38 routes, up from 37).

VERIFICATION DEBT
Not exercised against a real statement PDF or a deliberately unreadable
file - that is the next task's sub-task and needs a document to test with.
No test covers the route handler itself (no HTTP-level test harness
exists); the schema and the storage-before-extract ordering are the parts
covered.
